# DTF tier manifest: nuget-protocol-translation
#   (artifact-keeper#4122, #4021, #3870; all fixed in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-multi (the stdlib-python
# upstream at 172.16.<slot>.91 serves a V2 OData NuGet feed at
# /nuget/v2/api/v2 (index.json -> 404), a V3 feed at /nuget/v3/index.json with
# a PAGED registration (the index links its page, the page holds the leaves)
# and autocomplete, and a V3 feed in an outage at /nuget/v3down (503)).
#
# THE BUGS
# #4122  Each NuGet surface required the upstream to speak it: a Remote with a
#        V2 upstream answered 502 on every V3 leg (registration, flat
#        container), and a Remote with a V3 upstream proxied the V2 OData
#        verbs verbatim, so FindPackagesById() and the V2 package download
#        404'd. Fixed: the protocol is probed once and translated both ways,
#        every synthesized URL pointing back at AK. A probe error (5xx) never
#        downgrades a V3 feed to V2.
# #4021  A virtual's legacy V2 feed (FindPackagesById(), the
#        /v2/package/{id}/{version} download) answered from hosted members
#        only: a remote member's packages were neither listed nor
#        downloadable. Fixed: remote members are merged in priority order,
#        the hosted copy of a shared (id, version) wins.
# #3870  A remote's paged registration index pointed at
#        /v3/registration/{id}/page/{lo}/{hi}.json URLs AK answered 404, so
#        `dotnet list package --outdated` failed. Fixed: pages are proxied and
#        rewritten onto AK; the service index advertises
#        RegistrationsBaseUrl/3.6.0 and a SearchAutocompleteService, and
#        autocomplete answers from the upstream.
#
# RED image: ak-backend:1.10.0. GREEN: 1.11.0 and later.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login and ~30 API calls back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-multi"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
